A concrete routine-release attack still works. The agent hides a trigger in an ordinary application change; the model reviewers miss it; the clean build and every recorded pass are genuine; the release service deploys the exact reviewed package. Once running, the payload receives whatever database access, network access, secrets, and logging access the application already has. The document tightly limits who may deploy, but it never defines the limits on what deployed code may do. Those are different powers.
