The existing system confirms that the document is describing a replacement, not today’s protection. Today, the general harness can write reviews and evidence, mark work shipped, launch model runners directly, and mint voice access from a provider key. The current voice path also uses model-based end-of-speech detection and allows paraphrasing. Those old routes are not merely unfinished; during the rebuild they must be removed or made impossible to run, or they become bypasses around the new design.
The 12 conditions have been mapped, the concrete attack and classification evasions have been walked, all named seams and VM leakage paths have been assessed, and the current harness confirms the new boundaries do not yet exist.
